-- title:
--   Cotangent generation from separation of dual-number points
-- statement:
--   Let $O$ be a commutative local ring with residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,O$, and let $R$ be a commutative Noetherian local ring which is an $O$-algebra. Let $\mathrm{res}\colon R \to k$ be a ring homomorphism whose composite with the structure map $O \to R$ is the residue map of $O$. Let $s$ be a subset of the maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_R$. Assume the following separation hypothesis: for any two ring homomorphisms $\chi, \chi'\colon R \to k[\varepsilon]$ into the dual numbers over $k$, each satisfying that its composite with the projection $k[\varepsilon] \to k$ onto the first coordinate equals $\mathrm{res}$ and that its restriction along $O \to R$ is $o \mapsto \bar o + 0\cdot\varepsilon$ (the composite of the residue map of $O$ with the structure map $k \to k[\varepsilon]$), if $\chi(x) = \chi'(x)$ for all $x \in s$ then $\chi = \chi'$. The conclusion is the equality of ideals of $R$
--   $$\mathfrak m_R = \big(\mathfrak m_O \cdot R\big) + (s) + \mathfrak m_R^2,$$
--   where $\mathfrak m_O \cdot R$ denotes the image ideal of $\mathfrak m_O$ under $O \to R$, $(s)$ the ideal generated by $s$, and the right-hand side is the supremum of these three ideals.
--
--   This is the passage from a first-order (dual-number) uniqueness statement about points of a deformation functor to a statement about generators of the maximal ideal of a representing ring: tangent vectors at $\mathrm{res}$ are the $k$-linear functionals on the relative cotangent space $\mathfrak m_R/(\mathfrak m_O R + \mathfrak m_R^2)$, and separation by $s$ says that the classes of $s$ span it. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd part of the development to exhibit explicit generators of the maximal ideal of rings pro-representing deformation problems for special formal $O_D$-modules.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IsLocalRing_maximalIdeal_eq_map_sup_span_sup_sq_of_forall_ringHom_dualNumber_eqOn.lean

